ow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 98694 unstated crosses, 43772 join integers no single wing carries all three of — over two fifths and under a half, since 43772 × 5 > 98694 × 2 and 43772 × 2 < 98694.","statement":"((43772 * 5 > 98694 * 2) ∧ (43772 * 2 < 98694)) ∧ (43772 < 98694)","address":"5a6bb15f-0490-8a5a-bd53-84ad1c672362","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"43772 \\cdot 5 > 98694 \\cdot 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 43772 \\cdot 2 < 98694 \\quad\\land\\quad 43772 < 98694","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>43772</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>98694</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>43772</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>98694</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>43772</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>98694</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1530 formula-shaped statements carry 1458 distinct byte-strings and 1325 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1325 < 1458) ∧ (1530 - 1325 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"d864357f-234e-8e02-8b5c-d88fac4bb415","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1325 < 1458 \\quad\\land\\quad 1530 - 1325 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1325</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1458</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1530</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1325</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1530 formula-shaped statements across 115 wings are built from 780 distinct integers and state 453 crosses, against 98694 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 453 × 100 < 98694, at between 13 and 14 formulas per wing.","statement":"((453 * 100 < 98694) ∧ (780 > 115)) ∧ ((115 * 13 < 1530) ∧ (115 * 14 > 1530))","address":"f53af925-5488-8172-bf8c-a7aadaf3e0e1","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"453 \\cdot 100 < 98694 \\quad\\land\\quad 780 > 115 \\quad\\land\\quad 115 \\cdot 13 < 1530 \\quad\\land\\quad 115 \\cdot 14 > 1530","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>453</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>98694</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>780</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>115</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>115</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>115</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
